  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 Annual  NDSP2 report (using a designed web-based report) provided by Provincial DACs and DAWGs. 
1.2. Five Provincial DACs improved their function and disability coordination (average score of 5/5 )
1.3. # of  activity plan of annual action plan of five target PDACs in 2022 implemented
1.4 The draft new /amended disability law submitted to the Council of Ministers.
1.5. Number of persons with disabilities including women and girls with disabilities received public services through the coordination and referral support of five Provincial DACs</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">2,554 persons with disabilities (1,185 or 46% were women with disabilities)</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Annual NDSP2 report (using a designed web-based report) provided by Provincial DACs and DAWGs. 
- Five Provincial DACs improved their function and disability coordination (average score of 5/5 )
- 5 of activity plan of annual action plan of five target PDACs in 2022 implemented
- 2500 persons with disabilities (50% are women with disabilities) access to social service and social protection scheme 
- The draft new /amended disability law submitted to the Council of Ministers.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. DAC developed an Online Web Application Report on NDSP2 in July 2022 and trained 44 participants from line ministries and Provincial Disability Action Councils on data entry and reporting. As a result, 17 (38%) of the 44 line-ministries, institutions, and provincial disability action councils that provided nominated names for the NDSP2 report provided the NDSP2 progress report via the NDSP online web application.
2. The questionnaire developed was a Rubric Scale from 1 to 5 to evaluate the function of the five Provincial Disability Action Councils (PDACs). Level 1 denotes poor PDAC functionality or effectiveness, level 3 denotes moderate PDAC functionality or effectiveness, and level 5 denotes excellent PDAC functionality or effectiveness. Comparing March 2022 and October 2022, five PDACs improve their functions by 0.46/5 (3.33/5 in March 2022 to 3.79/5 in October 2022) after receiving capacity building and technical assistance from UNDP and DAC.
3. With technical support of UNDP, Five PDACS finalized the annual workplan for 2022 since January 2022 and implemented with the members, organizations of persons with disabilities and relevant stakeholders throughout the year.
4. Through the intervention and coordination of five PDACs from January to September 2022, 50,066 (25,324 women and girls with disabilities) persons with disabilities received the public services and social protection services including rehabilitation services, COVID-19 vaccination, disability identification interview, IDPoor cards, vocational training, employments, small business establishments, livelihood supports, food and sanitation and so on.
5. To ensure compliance with the United Nations Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, the revised disability law was finalized after extensive consultations with relevant stakeholders such as government line ministries, CSOs, OPDs, DPs, and the private sector (UNCRPD). The DAC and MoSVY will conduct an impact assessment of the revised disability law in early 2023 before submitting it to the Council of Minister in the middle of 2023.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
